 Every component's `<Component>/latest/src/` gains a **`thinglish/`** folder beside `ts/`, `js/`, `thinglish.ts/`, `thinglish.js/`, `puml/`, `mmd/`: the model **serialized in pure Thinglish** (the grammar above), one type per file — **`<Component>/latest/src/thinglish/EAM/<layer>/<Name>.class.thing`** or **`<Name>.interface.thing`** — rendered from the **model** by the M2 target **`M2ThingClass`** (never parsed from source), generated and committed like every target.
 
-- **TH1 one file per type, derived:** every catalogued class has exactly one `.thing` file of the right kind in its component's `<Component>/latest/src/thinglish/EAM/<layer>/`; expected set derived from the catalog (CHECKED / SKIPPED / TOTAL, SKIPPED 0); seed a missing or wrong-kind file → RED.
+### Pure Thinglish vs translation conventions (Tron, 2026-10-02 — plan of record [plans/2026-10-02-pure-thinglish-interfaces-and-inline-models.md](plans/2026-10-02-pure-thinglish-interfaces-and-inline-models.md), APPROVED in plan mode)
+
+> **Tron (verbatim):** "in pure thinglish there is no need for interfaces to be abstract classes. just if we translate it to typescript and javascript … also there is no need in thinglish to separate the attributes, properties, relationships and collections into a xyzModel, but list them on top of the class/interface in that order line by line before the methods."
+
+Pure Thinglish (`.thing`) shows the model as a modeller reads it. §1–§3 above (the `Interface` marker, interfaces as abstract classes, `static get implements()`, one type per file `X.class.*` / `X.interface.*`) and the separate `XModel` class are **translation conventions** for the TS/JS targets only. **Rendering only:** the model and every other target are byte-identical.
+
+1. **No `entry` keyword** — neither on classes nor interfaces (`isEntry` is a translation fact).
+2. **An interface is a plain `interface X`** — no `extends Interface` marker; `isAbstract` of an interface is **not a Thinglish fact** (ruling F6 below is superseded).
+3. **Inherited** attributes, properties, relationships and collections are **not listed** — silently inherited. An **override** that changes a member (e.g. a new initializer) is the class's OWN fact and is listed (`override attribute displayName = 'Web4 MDA'`).
+4. **A model bound by exactly ONE owner** is not its own `.thing`: its members are listed on top of the owner, whose header drops the `<XModel>` binding.
+5. **A model shared by several owners** (`ClassModel`, `FileModel`, `RelationshipModel`, `AttributeModel` — their owners are siblings) **renders as an interface** carrying its members; each owner `implements` it.
+6. **`ItemModel` renders as `interface ItemView extends View, Displayable`** with its attributes and properties.
+7. **`Model`, `TypedModel` and the standalone data models** (`ImportModel`, `ParameterModel`, `TypeAliasModel`, `TaggedProfileModel`, `ScenarioIndexModel`) **render as interfaces**.
+
+**Member order** (grammar `body`): all `attribute` lines, then `property`, then `relationship`, then `collection`, then methods — one per line.
+
+- **TH1 one file per type, derived:** ~~every catalogued class~~ **every catalogued class that pure Thinglish shows as a type (rulings 4–7: a 1:1 model has NO own file)** has exactly one `.thing` file of the right kind in its component's `<Component>/latest/src/thinglish/EAM/<layer>/`; expected set derived from the catalog (CHECKED / SKIPPED / TOTAL, SKIPPED 0); seed a missing or wrong-kind file → RED.
 - **TH2 generated from the model:** `npm start` reproduces every `.thing` with zero diff; seed a hand-edit → RED.
 - **TH3 lossless except EXACTLY the held set:** every model fact appears — namespace, dependencies, kind, type params, extends/implements, attributes (type, initializer, modifiers), properties, methods (type params, params incl. `...`/`?`/defaults, return type, modifiers, TypeScript body or `;`), relationships/collections (kind, `redefines`); seed: drop any one from the renderer → RED by name.
 - **TH4 only grammar keywords:** every keyword used in any `.thing` belongs to the keyword set **derived from `ThinglishGrammar`**, each mapped per SC8 (an M3 element, an instance of `Namespace`/`Version`, or an attribute of an M3 element).
 - **TH5 no invention:** a model fact the grammar cannot express is reported (the held table), never made up and never silently dropped.
+- **TH6 member order (NEW 2026-10-02):** in every `.thing` body the member kinds appear in grammar order; seed an out-of-order member → RED.
+- **TH7 rendering only (NEW 2026-10-02):** the change set touches only `*.thing`; every other target is byte-identical.
 - Parsing `.thing` back (`ThinglishParser`, F6) is out of scope — these files are its input.
 
 **Increments** (plan of record): **A** = this grammar + keyword rows + held table, `ThinglishGrammar` model, oopTester's SC8 extension — ONE atomic push. **B** = `M2ThingClass` + `<Component>/latest/src/thinglish/` for every component + TH1–TH5, with the target-listing tests' expectations as oopTester's patches.
